<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chhachhrauli</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Chhachhrauli is a town in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yamunanagar-district">Yamunanagar district</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haryana">Haryana</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. In the late 18th century it became the seat of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikhism">Sikh</a> chiefs of Kalsia, descendants of Gurbakhsh Singh of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karorsinghia-misl">Karorsinghia</a> misl, and remained the capital of the small princely state of Kalsia until it merged into independent India in 1948.</p></div>
